1
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:07,219
Well it is a chilly wet summer's day and we are gonna go up there.
这是个阴冷潮湿的夏日，我们要往那上面走。

2
00:00:07,219 --> 00:00:10,620
We're doing some solo alpine survival camping in bushcraft.
作者打算独自进行高山野外露营，运用户外技能。

3
00:00:11,219 --> 00:00:15,780
I don't have a tent and I'm gonna hike 17 miles up this mountain.
他没带帐篷，打算沿山徒步十七英里。

4
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:20,729
And we're gonna see if I can't build a shelter where there's no trees no firewood.
他想试试能否在没有树木、没有柴火的地方搭出庇护处。

5
00:00:20,739 --> 00:00:25,450
Also gonna hike to a remote alpine lake see if I can't catch some dinner.
还打算走到偏远高山湖泊，看看能否钓到晚餐。

6
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:30,969
And try not to get eaten by a bear.
还有，尽量别被熊吃掉。

7
00:00:30,979 --> 00:00:33,780
See this little plant right here it's called yarrow.
看眼前这株植物，作者称它为 yarrow。

8
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:39,370
It's a medicinal plant people make tea out of it for stomach aches.
他说这是一种药用植物，有人用来泡茶缓解胃痛。

9
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:45,530
This plant right here this is fireweed the blossoms are edible.
这另一株他叫 fireweed，并称花朵可以食用。

10
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:50,410
A little bit like honeysuckle here in alaska a lot of people like to make jelly out of the blossoms.
他说有点像金银花，在阿拉斯加，很多人用这些花做果冻。

11
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:54,649
There's a mama moose and two babies right over there down in the valley.
山谷下面那边有一头母驼鹿和两头幼崽。

12
00:00:54,659 --> 00:00:58,579
A lot of moose in this area the moose feed on this willowed.
这地区驼鹿很多，作者说它们吃这里的柳类植物；原字幕植物词待听辨。

13
00:00:58,579 --> 00:01:08,410
You can see how it's all clipped and broken that's from moose grazing and biting the tips off.
可以看到枝条被啃断的痕迹，作者说那是驼鹿吃草、咬掉嫩梢留下的。

14
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:13,289
See right here blueberry bushes down here are crowberry bushes.
这里是他所说的蓝莓灌木，下面则是岩高兰灌木。

15
00:01:13,299 --> 00:01:15,609
There's a crowberry forming.
这里正在长出一颗岩高兰果实。

16
00:01:15,619 --> 00:01:20,969
Pretty much anywhere in this valley that's not covered with trees is has berry bushes.
这山谷里，没被树木覆盖的地方几乎都长着浆果灌木。

17
00:01:20,979 --> 00:01:22,500
But we're too early for berries.
不过我们来得太早，还没到浆果成熟的时候。

18
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:26,100
Come here in the early fall you can fill up buckets of berries.
作者说初秋来时，浆果多到能装满一桶桶。

19
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:34,490
And the bears will be out here feeding on berries as well.
熊也会在这里吃浆果。

20
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:38,580
You can see we still have unmelted snow up here it's a bit chillier up here.
你能看到这里还有未融化的雪，上面更冷一点。

21
00:01:38,580 --> 00:01:47,290
In the mountains the weather moves quick and weather forecasts aren't very accurate in the mountains got to be prepared.
作者说山中天气变化快，预报不总准确，所以需要有所准备。

22
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:51,050
Look at that cloud coming around the mountain it's coming so quick.
看那片绕山而来的云，移动得真快。

23
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:57,850
The weather and visibility can change in a heartbeat in the mountains.
山中的天气和能见度可能转眼间就变。

24
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:27,020
I'm getting a little sweaty now I gotta go climb this thing uh.
我开始有点出汗了，得继续往上爬。

25
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:40,250
All right we just went over the top of our first mountain about 3 500 feet of elevation.
我们翻过了第一座山，大约到达三千五百英尺海拔。

26
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:46,900
And you can see here we got this little saddle and another mountain and another mountain and they just keep getting bigger and bigger.
这里有个小山鞍，又一座山、再一座山，而且越来越高大。

27
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:51,060
By the way look at these valleys see how they're just like perfect bowl shapes.
顺便看这些山谷，形状简直像完美的碗。

28
00:02:51,060 --> 00:03:00,170
They're like used instead of the v's you see out east these were all carved by glaciers.
作者说，它们像 U 形，不像东边那些 V 形谷，是冰川雕刻出来的。

29
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:06,089
But right there is a parky squirrel parky squirrels and tarmigan are about the only game you'll find up here.
那儿有只作者称的地松鼠，他说高处大概只能见到这种松鼠和雷鸟等猎物。

30
00:03:06,099 --> 00:03:11,850
And uh parky squirrels don't taste very good it's like eating buffalo wings with claws and fur.
他开玩笑说，松鼠不好吃，像带爪子、带毛的辣鸡翅。
